2:[["$","div",null,{"className":"aeo-answer tl-dr","children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Quick Answer:"}]," A CLAT 2027 study plan should span 6-10 months across five sections — English Language, Current Affairs & GK, Legal Reasoning, Logical Reasoning, and Quantitative Techniques. The new CLAT pattern (comprehension-based) means you should spend 60-70% of your time reading and 30-40% solving. Study 5-7 hours daily, prioritizing Legal Reasoning (highest weightage, ~25%) and Current Affairs. Use an AI planner like PlanBot to rotate sections daily, schedule daily newspaper reading, and track sectional accuracy."]}]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"Why CLAT 2027 Demands a Different Strategy"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"CLAT (Common Law Admission Test) is the gateway to the 24 National Law Universities (NLUs) and one of India's most competitive entrance exams — over 70,000 aspirants compete for roughly 4,000 seats across the top NLUs."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"The exam changed in 2020"}],", and the new pattern trips up most first-time aspirants. Instead of standalone factual questions, CLAT is now ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"entirely comprehension-based"}],". Every section gives you a 450-word passage, then asks 4-6 questions derived from it. This rewards ",["$","em",null,{"children":"reading speed and comprehension"}]," over rote memorization."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"That's why a generic \"study hard\" approach fails. You need a plan that:"}],"\n",["$","ol",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":["Builds ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"daily reading stamina"}]," (the exam is 120 passages in 2 hours)"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":["Rotates ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"all five sections"}]," so none gets neglected"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":["Allocates time for ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"daily current affairs"}]," (newspaper + monthly compendium)"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":["Builds in ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"weekly mock tests"}]," with analysis"]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"An AI study planner like PlanBot handles all four automatically — you just tell it your target, and it builds the schedule."}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"The CLAT 2027 Exam Pattern"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Before planning, understand what you're optimizing for:"}],"\n",["$","table",null,{"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th",null,{"children":"Section"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"Passages"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"Questions"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"Weightage"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"Difficulty"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"English Language"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"5-6"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"22-26"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"~20%"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Medium"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Current Affairs & GK"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"5-6"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"28-32"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"~25%"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"High"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Legal Reasoning"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"5-6"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"28-32"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"~25%"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"High"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Logical Reasoning"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"4-5"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"22-26"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"~20%"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Medium"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Quantitative Techniques"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"3-4"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"13-17"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"~10%"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Low"}]]}]]}]]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Total:"}]," ~120 questions · 120 marks · 2 hours · Negative marking of 0.25 per wrong answer."]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"The 8-Month CLAT 2027 Master Plan"}],"\n",["$","h3",null,{"children":"Phase 1: Foundation (Months 1-3)"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Objective:"}]," Build reading habit + clear conceptual basics"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Daily Study Target:"}]," 5-6 hours"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"Section Split:"}]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"English & Reading Comprehension: 1.5 hours/day"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Legal Reasoning (concepts): 1 hour/day"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Logical Reasoning (concepts): 1 hour/day"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Current Affairs + newspaper: 1 hour/day"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Quant basics: 30-45 min/day"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"Key Actions:"}]}],"\n",["$","ol",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":["Read ",["$","em",null,{"children":"The Hindu"}]," or ",["$","em",null,{"children":"Indian Express"}]," editorial daily — this is non-negotiable"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Start reading 30-40 pages of non-fiction daily to build stamina"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Complete a Legal Reasoning foundation book (Universal's or AP Bhardwaj)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Solve 10-15 Logical Reasoning questions daily"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Revise Quant fundamentals (Class 10 level: percentages, ratios, time-speed, DI)"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"How PlanBot Helps:"}]," Tell PlanBot ",["$","em",null,{"children":"\"I'm preparing for CLAT 2027, starting fresh. I can study 6 hours daily. I'm weak in Legal Reasoning and Current Affairs.\""}]," The AI creates a daily schedule that front-loads your weak sections during peak focus hours and blocks fixed time for newspaper reading."]}],"\n",["$","h3",null,{"children":"Phase 2: Intensive Practice (Months 4-6)"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Objective:"}]," Build sectional mastery + start sectional mocks"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Daily Study Target:"}]," 6-7 hours"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"What Changes:"}]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Shift from \"learning concepts\" to \"solving passages\""}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Start 1 sectional mock per week (alternating sections)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Read 2-3 comprehension passages daily across sections"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Start a Current Affairs compendium (monthly magazine + notes)"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"Section-Wise Focus:"}]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"English:"}]," Practice inference-based questions, vocabulary in context"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Legal Reasoning:"}]," Focus on constitutional law, criminal law, torts, contracts"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Logical Reasoning:"}]," Critical reasoning (strengthen/weaken arguments) — this is the highest-ROI area"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Current Affairs:"}]," Maintain a daily diary of events from the last 10 months"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Quant:"}]," Practice Data Interpretation sets (this is where quant questions come from)"]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"How PlanBot Helps:"}]," ",["$","em",null,{"children":"\"I have my first sectional mock next Sunday. This week, prioritize Logical Reasoning and 2 hours of mock practice.\""}]," PlanBot adjusts your week dynamically."]}],"\n",["$","h3",null,{"children":"Phase 3: Mock & Revision (Months 7-8)"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Objective:"}]," Full-length mocks + error analysis + speed building"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Daily Study Target:"}]," 7-8 hours"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"What Changes:"}]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"3-4 full-length mocks per week (under timed conditions)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Deep error analysis after every mock (this is where scores jump)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Revise your Current Affairs diary daily"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Reduce new learning; focus on consolidation"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"The Mock Routine:"}]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Monday: Mock test (2 hours) + analysis (2 hours)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Tuesday-Thursday: Fix weak areas identified in analysis"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Friday: Light revision + newspaper"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Saturday: Mock test + analysis"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Sunday: Full revision + rest"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"How PlanBot Helps:"}]," PlanBot creates a mock-centric schedule in this phase. Tell it your mock scores and it rebalances — ",["$","em",null,{"children":"\"I scored 72/120, lost 12 marks in Legal Reasoning passages\""}]," → PlanBot allocates more Legal Reasoning drills the following week."]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"Subject-Wise Strategy Deep Dive"}],"\n",["$","h3",null,{"children":"English Language"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"The trap: students think English is \"easy\" and ignore it. Don't. This section rewards consistent daily reading over months."}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Daily:"}]," 30 min reading newspaper editorial + 1 comprehension passage"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Weekly:"}]," 2 passages from a CLAT-specific English book"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Monthly:"}]," Read one full non-fiction book (biographies, history, science)"]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","h3",null,{"children":"Current Affairs & GK"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["This is the section that ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"kills most aspirants"}]," because it feels unpredictable. The secret: consistency beats last-minute cramming every time."]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Daily:"}]," 45 min newspaper (front page + national + editorial + sports/business highlights)"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Weekly:"}]," 1 hour reviewing a current affairs magazine"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Monthly:"}]," Create a one-page summary of key events"]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["CLAT focuses on the ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"last 10-12 months"}]," of events. If you maintain a daily diary, revision in the last month takes hours, not weeks."]}],"\n",["$","h3",null,{"children":"Legal Reasoning"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["The highest-weightage section and the one most aspirants underestimate. CLAT legal reasoning tests ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"principle-application"}],", not memorization."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"You get a legal principle + a factual situation. You must apply the principle to the facts."}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Focus areas: Constitutional Law, Criminal Law, Law of Torts, Law of Contracts, General Legal Maxims"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Practice 10-15 principle-application questions daily"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":["Don't memorize; understand ",["$","em",null,{"children":"how to apply principles"}]]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","h3",null,{"children":"Logical Reasoning"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["Two types: Analytical (arrangements, puzzles) and Critical (arguments, assumptions). CLAT leans heavily on ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"critical reasoning"}],"."]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Practice strengthen/weaken/inference questions daily"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"This is the most learnable section — accuracy improves fast with practice"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Aim for 90%+ accuracy here"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","h3",null,{"children":"Quantitative Techniques"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Lowest weightage (~10%) but high ROI if you're comfortable with Class 10 math."}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Focus entirely on Data Interpretation (tables, graphs, pie charts)"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Master percentages, ratios, averages, profit-loss, time-speed-distance"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Don't over-invest — spending 3 hours/day here is a strategic mistake"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"How to Use PlanBot for CLAT — A Practical Workflow"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"PlanBot is free to start (2 AI plans/day) and built specifically for goal-based planning like exam prep. Here's the exact workflow:"}],"\n",["$","ol",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Set your goal:"}]," Download PlanBot, select the ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Student"}]," persona, and tell the AI: ",["$","em",null,{"children":"\"I'm preparing for CLAT 2027, exam in December. I can study 6 hours daily on weekdays and 8 hours on weekends. I'm weak in Legal Reasoning and Current Affairs.\""}]]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Get your daily plan:"}]," PlanBot generates a time-blocked schedule — say, 7-8:30am newspaper reading, 9-11am Legal Reasoning practice, 11:30am-1pm Logical Reasoning, evening English comprehension, with breaks built in."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Adjust when life happens:"}]," Missed a session? PlanBot reschedules automatically. ",["$","em",null,{"children":"\"I have a college fest this weekend\""}]," → PlanBot compresses the plan without dropping any section."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Track with streaks:"}]," The gamification (streaks, XP) is genuinely useful for CLAT prep — maintaining a 100-day reading streak is exactly the consistency you need."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Use the weekly AI report (Elite+):"}]," See where you actually spent time vs. where you planned to. This mirrors the self-analysis that toppers do."]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"Common CLAT Preparation Mistakes to Avoid"}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Ignoring English and Quant"}]," because they seem \"easy\" — these are easy marks you're throwing away"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Cramming Current Affairs in the last month"}]," — impossible to cover 12 months in 30 days"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Not doing enough mocks"}]," — mocks are where your score actually improves"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Skipping mock analysis"}]," — taking a mock without analyzing errors is wasted effort"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Over-studying Quant"}]," — 10% weightage doesn't deserve 30% of your time"]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"Frequently Asked Questions"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Can I crack CLAT in 6 months?"}]," Yes, if you can study 7-8 hours daily and stay consistent. The comprehension-based pattern is learnable faster than the old factual pattern, but you need serious daily reading practice."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"How many CLAT mocks should I solve?"}]," Aim for 40-50 full-length mocks in your prep cycle, with the majority in the last 3 months. Each mock needs 2 hours of analysis."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Is coaching necessary for CLAT?"}]," Not strictly. Many toppers are self-prepared. What matters is consistency, the right material, and a structured plan — which an AI planner provides."]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"Start Planning for CLAT 2027 Today"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"CLAT is winnable for anyone who plans well and executes daily. The difference between a top-NLU seat and a missed opportunity is rarely intelligence — it's whether you had a plan and stuck to it."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=cpm.planbot","children":"Get PlanBot free on Android"}]," and let the AI build your CLAT 2027 study schedule today."]}]]
